O statistics to develop international education indicators, and to analyze the state of education worldwide. Yet experts at UNESCO estimate that data from perhaps 70 countries i slightly less than half of UNESCO's member states -- suffer serious reliability problems (UNESCO staff, personal interviews, 12-13 November 1992).


